\ by-intro: and by-exact (plan FE1g-4; docs/design/FE1G_TACTICS.md 2.4).
\ Lean: theorem self_imp (p : Prop) : p → p := by intro h; exact h
\ gives fun (p : Prop) (h : p) => h (tests/front/tactic-run.lean, t4).
\ Natural LeanForth cannot write Prop and -> yet (plan FE2), and the
\ statement's numeral and + are not elaborated yet (plans FE1e5, S2): the
\ text stops at end with error 139, exit 2. tests/front/tactic-basic.fs runs it with stand-ins
\ that give the statement forall (p : Prop), p -> p (whatever the words
\ below say) and elaborate h as the hypothesis; the kernel accepts it.
theorem self_imp
  Nat explicit: n
  0 n + n =
:= by
  by-intro: h
  h by-exact
end self_imp
